Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Yandex Browser — off-store force-install via ExtensionSettings.
; Yandex Browser supports Chromium group policies (unlike Opera / Opera GX, which support none).
; Policy root is the standard Yandex ADMX namespace — verify at browser://policy after applying.
; 1. Replace the ID with your 32-char ID (chars a-p only).
; 2. Replace the update_url with your own update manifest.
; 3. Use ExtensionSettings OR ExtensionInstallForcelist, never both (they double-deliver).
; 4. 32-bit browser? Also add the same keys under ...\SOFTWARE\WOW6432Node\Policies\YandexBrowser.
; Off-store force-install may also need the device to look managed (fake-mdm.reg), same as Chrome.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\YandexBrowser\ExtensionSettings]
"cbmpaamhmhdhnkofemgdlnbdadbpmjkn"="{\"installation_mode\":\"force_installed\",\"update_url\":\"https://sketchystan1.github.io/uBlock/update.xml\"}"

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\YandexBrowser]
"DeveloperToolsAvailability"=dword:00000001
